# Dart/Flutter — practices, tests, and tooling

## Dart

- Follow Effective Dart and `analysis_options.yaml`; use clear naming and single responsibility.
- Handle errors explicitly; keep strong null safety; avoid unchecked `!`.
- Document public APIs with `///` when useful.

## Flutter / UI

- Keep widgets cohesive and render-focused; use `const` when possible.
- For long lists, use `ListView.builder` or `SliverList`; avoid heavy work inside `build()`.

## Tests

- Use Arrange-Act-Assert; prioritize domain and bloc/cubit tests for critical rules.
- For UI tests, validate behavior per state; prefer fakes/stubs when practical.

## Logging

- Do not use loose `print`; use the project logging strategy.

## Codegen

- Never edit `*.g.dart` manually; after `@JsonSerializable` changes, regenerate with `build_runner`.

## Dependencies

- Add new packages only with clear value and technical justification.

## Final checklist

Compatible with domain instructions in [`.github/copilot-instructions.md`](.github/copilot-instructions.md)? Duplications removed, widget size controlled, UI/business separation, and BLoC usage reviewed?
